{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Moses fled from before it.</b> For it was then a fully actual serpent in pursuit. But the staffs of the sorcerers, for all their crocodile forms, had no motion in them — since sorcery does not produce anything truly existing in nature, as the Sages of blessed memory said (Sanhedrin 67b): 'A sorcerer cannot create even a camel.' Therefore Scripture says, וְהַמַּטֶּה אֲשֶׁר נֶהְפַּךְ לְנָחָשׁ (Exodus 7:15), and does not say 'to a תַּנִּין.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:18.282881263Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}